670	/****************************************************************************
671	 * Name: board_app_initialize
672	 *
673	 * Description:
674	 *   Perform application specific initialization.  This function is never
675	 *   called directly from application code, but only indirectly via the
676	 *   (non-standard) boardctl() interface using the command BOARDIOC_INIT.
677	 *
678	 * Input Parameters:
679	 *   arg - The boardctl() argument is passed to the board_app_initialize()
680	 *         implementation without modification.  The argument has no
681	 *         meaning to NuttX; the meaning of the argument is a contract
682	 *         between the board-specific initialization logic and the
683	 *         matching application logic.  The value could be such things as a
684	 *         mode enumeration value, a set of DIP switch settings, a
685	 *         pointer to configuration data read from a file or serial FLASH,
686	 *         or whatever you would like to do with it.  Every implementation
687	 *         should accept zero/NULL as a default configuration.
688	 *
689	 * Returned Value:
690	 *   Zero (OK) is returned on success; a negated errno value is returned on
691	 *   any failure to indicate the nature of the failure.
692	 *
693	 ****************************************************************************/
694	
695	int board_app_initialize(uintptr_t arg)
